  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1050 PM CDT Sun Jul 19 2026\n\nA cold front will push through late Tuesday night into Wednesday,\nbringing cooler and drier air into the region. This should lead to\na noticeable break from the heat and humidity, with highs falling\ninto the mid 80s and lower rain chances for the middle of the\nweek. Conditions turn much quieter overall after the active start\nto the week. \n\nHighs gradually moderate back into the upper 80s to low 90s by\nlate week and over the weekend. There is some potential for \nanother shortwave to spark scattered showers and storms around \nFriday into Friday night, though details remain uncertain at this \ntime. By next Monday, the pattern stays generally seasonal, with \nonly modest chances for diurnal thunderstorms.",
